            "review_title": "Review at Banh Duc Nom",
            "review_text": "blaughlan\nNewcastle, Australia134 contributions\n0\nAn overlooked gem\nMay 2018 • Couples\nMost tourists would walk past this hole-in-the-wall food stall without a second look, perhaps other than to wonder what it is they sell!\nWe have been to Hanoi numerous times and often walked past ourselves but on our latest trip were convinced to try their fare and I must say it was a revelation.\n\nNot sure what it is made of but the thick, gluey texture of the main part of the dish is a challenge to come to terms with. It is covered with a beautiful sauce which tastes like meat pie filling and is then topped off with your choice of fresh herbs. Filling and beautifully satisfying.\n\nDo yourself a favour and stop and try it. We certainly will when we return.\nAt around 10,000 VND it is a tasty bargain.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 23, 2018",
